  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Hi There!\n\nSo VRChat was updated yesterday,\n\n\"Fixes have been made to PhysBones to address jitter that was introduced in 2025.1.3.\n\n- These changes affected many avatars, but were most noticeable on a few skirt setups as well as long flow bones like flow toys. These changes also address an underlying jitter issue that were present in older versions but only under high framerate situations, greater than 60fps.\n\n- Please test your PhysBone creations and report any new or unfixed issues!\"\n\nI was on Monday night, where i was still experiencing the jitter issue to my avatar. Wasn't a huge deal to me, wanted it fixed but still.\n\nI was not on Tuesday night, but I was on Wednesday/Yesterday.\n\nWhen ever I turn side to side or move irregularly my clothes/hair PhysBones reset. I thought it was just me, until someone who purchased the avatar and previously posted pictures positively previously, also texted me via my ticket system. Saying they were having the same issue, and included a video which I linked. I also had my quest friends take a look at this issue to see if it was only PC sided, which it was not.\n\nNeither of us have updated our avatars since the update to make this occur in unity. I included videos before the update with the jitter, and ones afterward that show the bug and effects. Any help would be great!\n\nI was asked to create a bug report here, and also to include my PhysBone settings, so here you go!",
